{
 "_comment": "BM25-RBF (rcdl/bm25.py): the growing RBF layer with sparse Okapi BM25 key matching in place of the dot product, kappa = exp(gamma (S(q,k) - S(q,q)) / S(q,q)), gamma = sqrt(d)/T (the RBF kernel exactly when S is the dot product). One pass, the paper's single-pass setting (L = 2, batch 16, T = 10, eta = 10; RBF 59.10 +- 0.62 over 5 seeds, Muon 57.41 +- 0.52). Defaults: m = 1024 terms per vector (top |coordinates| of a random rotation, split by sign), k1 = 1.2, b = 0.75, live IDF. Ablations: m, rotation, IDF, saturation (k1 -> inf, b = 0), temperature (gamma), value rate. *_10ep: 10 epochs, batch 64, augmentation (RBF 63.39, Muon 62.22).",
 "defaults": {
  "eval_every": 1000000,
  "eval_subset": 2000,
  "eval_batch_size": 250
